# model.pins , the exact weights a box runs: name, SHA-256, bytes, where they come from.
#
# Read by tools/setup_llama.sh (a download or a copied file is accepted only if it matches),
# tools/stage_models.sh (the same check before staging) and tools/models_check.sh (what an
# installed box has, and --fix to replace what does not match). The mirror (tools/mirror_fetch.sh)
# carries the same files under its signed manifest; the pins here are the second, independent
# statement of what "the model" is, so a Hugging Face upload that changes under the same name
# (Unsloth's mmproj did, before their F32 patch_embd fix) is caught wherever the bytes come from.
#
# Gemma 4 12B, Unsloth's GGUF build (Apache 2.0, no account, no token):
#   https://huggingface.co/unsloth/gemma-4-12b-it-GGUF
#
# name  sha256  bytes  upstream
gemma-4-12b-it-Q4_K_M.gguf  0a270ec9fe6b34f4a0d33992b6135117b484ebc4766ab76b51d4ae8c457e4c42  7121861440  https://huggingface.co/unsloth/gemma-4-12b-it-GGUF/resolve/main/gemma-4-12b-it-Q4_K_M.gguf
mmproj-F16.gguf             91f086971e56d7a7d8d39e271873fccdb49541bd259d6e02c401a4f1cb7a219e  175115840   https://huggingface.co/unsloth/gemma-4-12b-it-GGUF/resolve/main/mmproj-F16.gguf
# The embedder, EmbeddingGemma 300M QAT Q8_0 (Gemma Terms of Use, which travel with it): the mirror
# carries it in set `embeddings` under its signed manifest. Its pin line goes here, from the manifest:
#   curl -s https://www.localghost.ai/mirror/MANIFEST.txt | grep /embeddings/
# as: embeddinggemma-300m-qat-Q8_0.gguf  <sha256>  <bytes>  <upstream url>
# Until then it is accepted from the mirror (signed) or a file you provide, and the older
# embeddinggemma-300m-q8.gguf a box already has keeps working.
